x01-core-alignment patch 01-particle-mass (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (h) Particle mass.

SAGE26 behaviour: R0 runs with PartMass 0.086 (R/input/millennium.par:41 "PartMass        0.086";
R0, SAGE26's input/millennium.par with its six physics switches off, keeps that line, and the R0
output header attribute Header/Simulation/particle_mass is 0.086). SAGE26 reads it as a
double (R/src/core_read_parameter_file.c:161) and forms the virial mass of a subhalo, or of a FoF central
whose catalogue Mvir is negative, as Len * PartMass (R/src/model_halo_properties.c:31-36).

Mimic behaviour replaced: the mini-Millennium package declares particle_mass 0.0860657
(simulations/mini-millennium/simulation_info.yaml:20-23), read into MimicConfig.PartMass
(src/core/read_parameter_file.c:1043-1047) and used by the same rule, Len * MimicConfig.PartMass
(src/core/virial.c:47-53).

What the patch changes: particle_mass value 0.0860657 -> 0.086 in
simulations/mini-millennium/simulation_info.yaml. Nothing else.

Reading for i02: yes, it would change sage16's and halos-only's output on mini-Millennium. The value
belongs to the simulation package, which every model built with SIMULATION=mini-millennium reads, and
the core virial rule (src/core/virial.c:47-53) feeds Mvir, Rvir and Vvir of every subhalo (and of any
central with a negative catalogue mass) in every package, and all physics downstream of them.

diff --git a/simulations/mini-millennium/simulation_info.yaml b/simulations/mini-millennium/simulation_info.yaml
index 8276c17c..52031031 100644
--- a/simulations/mini-millennium/simulation_info.yaml
+++ b/simulations/mini-millennium/simulation_info.yaml
@@ -18,6 +18,6 @@ simulation:
     units: Mpc/h
     h_convention: carried
   particle_mass:
-    value: 0.0860657
+    value: 0.086
     units: 1e10 Msun/h
     h_convention: carried
